# steps/table-receiver.md §10: the part unit_s7_part_forward_part.lm2 (harness Parts) declares later ahead of
# its definition.  A part is read as the source is, each item against its own root, so the declaration binds
# to the definition in the part (read against the source's root it binds nothing, and the definition is a
# second one: "duplicate definition").  early(40) is 43.  Entry 7.
int: r 0
r: early(40)
if: r != 43
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
